WEBVTT

00:00:11.830 --> 00:00:14.710
Good morning. You're up early, as usual.

00:00:14.710 --> 00:00:16.460
It's already 9 o'clock, you know.

00:00:16.460 --> 00:00:18.540
Kylie and the rest of 
them are still out cold.

00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:22.040
I take it you all must have 
stayed out well after I left.

00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:23.800
We gotta enjoy ourselves 
every once in a while.

00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:27.040
Especially after dealing with 
our last bit of "cargo".

00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:28.920
Plus we all got a nice hefty bonus, too.

00:00:29.290 --> 00:00:30.420
I suppose that's true.

00:00:30.790 --> 00:00:31.460
What?

00:00:31.460 --> 00:00:34.830
I was just thinking how much
our tenacious Reona has changed.

00:00:34.830 --> 00:00:37.080
Especially since I first 
met you back in Sapo.

00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:38.930
Spare me your sentimentality.

00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:45.920
Rahama is up in flames?

00:00:45.920 --> 00:00:48.380
And we're not talking small 
flames. What should we do?

00:00:48.380 --> 00:00:51.750
Rahama control tower, this 
is the Hagoromo, come in.

00:00:51.750 --> 00:00:52.580
Repeat...

00:00:52.580 --> 00:00:53.580
What does the Madame have to say?

00:00:53.580 --> 00:00:57.290
Well, see she told me never to wake her up
unless we're under attack, so...

00:00:57.290 --> 00:00:58.500
I'll head for the bridge straight away.

00:00:58.500 --> 00:00:59.540
Make it quick!

00:00:59.540 --> 00:01:01.420
You'll wanna wake up the others, right?

00:01:01.420 --> 00:01:02.540
Can you do that for me?

00:01:03.040 --> 00:01:04.540
But only after you get some clothes on.

00:01:04.880 --> 00:01:05.960
Hmm?

00:01:17.710 --> 00:01:23.210
The Magnificent
KOTOBUKI

00:01:24.540 --> 00:01:27.710
Flying through the mesh of clouds

00:01:27.830 --> 00:01:31.250
Our dancing wings wrap up in the wind

00:01:31.250 --> 00:01:34.710
Stars fall right before our eyes

00:01:40.710 --> 00:01:44.000
The blue of all blues that drew us in

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:47.080
We kicked up off the blurring ground

00:01:47.330 --> 00:01:52.290
Let me hear the sound of the sky you know

00:01:54.880 --> 00:02:01.630
Take flight make gravity your ally

00:02:01.750 --> 00:02:08.000
One more time, however many 
times, laughing all along

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:15.040
We would never look back when we fly

00:02:15.040 --> 00:02:20.250
An everlasting dream we 
live in pursuit of tomorrow

00:02:20.380 --> 00:02:23.750
Amid rising despair I locked away my love

00:02:23.750 --> 00:02:26.080
I hate my weak self

00:02:26.790 --> 00:02:32.040
Here and now passes by as 
we head towards the future

00:02:36.010 --> 00:02:39.970
Rahama's Longest Day

00:02:36.920 --> 00:02:39.970
Well, it's hard to imagine anything worse
than being struck by calamity.

00:02:39.970 --> 00:02:42.430
But we were fortunate enough to get
all the fires put out without a hitch.

00:02:42.430 --> 00:02:44.330
There wasn't even a single casualty.

00:02:44.330 --> 00:02:48.330
All thanks to the firefighters and
our vigilante force. How splendid!

00:02:48.330 --> 00:02:49.960
There's nothing "splendid" about this at all!

00:02:49.500 --> 00:02:51.830
That was where the vigilante force
was stationed, wasn't it?

00:02:49.960 --> 00:02:50.830
There isn't?

00:02:51.830 --> 00:02:53.250
Did someone start a fire?

00:02:53.250 --> 00:02:54.250
Sheesh.

00:02:54.250 --> 00:02:57.460
This is just the sorta thing I'd expect
from you, you bunch of idiots.

00:02:57.460 --> 00:02:58.460
Who do you think you're talking to?

00:02:58.460 --> 00:03:01.210
I come from a long, honorable 
line of paupers, you know!

00:03:01.210 --> 00:03:02.540
Is that a friend of Chika's?

00:03:02.540 --> 00:03:05.790
Hey! That's the guy who picked a fight with her
and got aero-slammed into a pulp!

00:03:05.790 --> 00:03:08.580
I was just going easy on you,
'cause you were all hurt and stuff!

00:03:08.580 --> 00:03:10.750
I'd never lose if I was 
actually trying to win!

00:03:10.750 --> 00:03:12.080
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:03:12.080 --> 00:03:14.920
But are you really gonna pick 
a fight with me right now?

00:03:14.920 --> 00:03:16.790
This is 12.7mm ammunition.

00:03:15.540 --> 00:03:18.380
After you went and let 
your offices burn down?

00:03:16.790 --> 00:03:18.800
A repacked junk shell.

00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:20.460
The sort that air pirates tend to use.

00:03:20.460 --> 00:03:21.380
Air pirates?!

00:03:21.380 --> 00:03:22.920
Oh no, they weren't pirates.

00:03:22.920 --> 00:03:25.010
They called themselves "Elite Industries".

00:03:25.010 --> 00:03:26.420
What a ridiculous name.

00:03:26.420 --> 00:03:28.290
They still attacked you though, didn't they?

00:03:28.290 --> 00:03:30.330
Aren't you guys supposed to be vigilantes?

00:03:30.330 --> 00:03:32.380
You just let them pummel you
without even fighting back?

00:03:32.380 --> 00:03:35.210
All of us bravely fought as best we could!

00:03:35.210 --> 00:03:37.830
But our valiant efforts were for naught
and we exhausted all our options!

00:03:37.830 --> 00:03:39.290
So you lost, then.

00:03:39.290 --> 00:03:40.540
Tell us everything that happened.

00:03:41.540 --> 00:03:44.830
We've got... one, two, three...

00:03:44.830 --> 00:03:47.000
Just a whole bunch of incoming bogeys!

00:03:51.370 --> 00:03:54.790
Howdy, howdy, good folks of Rahama!

00:03:54.790 --> 00:03:56.580
We are Elite Industries.

00:03:56.580 --> 00:03:58.960
Elite Industries, I say!

00:03:58.960 --> 00:04:00.460
An inferno of hardships

00:03:59.210 --> 00:04:00.670
Have no fear!

00:04:00.460 --> 00:04:02.960
Spurting blood billowing up from a sandy pit

00:04:00.670 --> 00:04:03.040
We'll just be borrowing your runway here!

00:04:02.960 --> 00:04:06.420
We'll chase you to the ends of this world

00:04:03.170 --> 00:04:05.880
Thank you for your cooperation!

00:04:06.420 --> 00:04:10.310
There's no use running

00:04:10.310 --> 00:04:14.080
Oh we are a company, we are no air pirates

00:04:14.460 --> 00:04:18.650
Come along chosen ones, you are the elite

00:04:18.650 --> 00:04:22.290
Elite industries

00:04:26.960 --> 00:04:29.710
Howdy, howdy! Pleasure to meet ya, Mr. Mayor!

00:04:29.710 --> 00:04:34.830
The name's Torihei,
and I'm the president and CEO of Elite Industries.

00:04:34.830 --> 00:04:37.980
Truth is, we're here with a once in a lifetime sort


00:04:37.980 --> 00:04:41.370
of business proposal to 
share with you all today!

00:04:41.370 --> 00:04:42.170
What sort of proposal?

00:04:42.170 --> 00:04:44.060
Yes, well you see, I've 
heard word that this town

00:04:44.060 --> 00:04:46.220
of yours has one fine 
fighter plane tucked away.

00:04:47.420 --> 00:04:49.130
Oh, you mean our Raiden?

00:04:49.130 --> 00:04:49.880
So it's true?!

00:04:49.880 --> 00:04:50.750
Mr. Mayor!

00:04:50.750 --> 00:04:53.670
Our company started off as 
a simple logistics company.

00:04:53.670 --> 00:04:56.400
But we've since adopted a 
corporate mission to innovate

00:04:56.400 --> 00:04:59.020
via concepts, technologies, 
and entrepreneurship.

00:04:59.040 --> 00:05:01.960
And now we have been striving
to make contributions to cultural endeavors.

00:05:01.960 --> 00:05:06.210
Using our fleet of now more than 40 fighters
to spread culture far and wide.

00:05:06.210 --> 00:05:08.460
But we still don't have 
all the manpower we need.

00:05:08.460 --> 00:05:12.000
And we were looking around for just the right
sort of fighter plane to do the job, see...

00:05:12.000 --> 00:05:14.870
When we heard that just such 
a craft might be found here,

00:05:14.870 --> 00:05:17.590
we came out to see if we might strike a deal!

00:05:17.590 --> 00:05:22.670
Of course we're willing to make a trade of comparable,
if not even more value!

00:05:22.670 --> 00:05:24.420
Ta-da!

00:05:24.880 --> 00:05:26.380
You want us to trade our Raiden for that?

00:05:26.380 --> 00:05:29.180
The ukiyo-e that were 
once brought over by the

00:05:29.180 --> 00:05:31.830
Yufang still fetch a high 
price among collectors.

00:05:31.830 --> 00:05:33.260
And this here is an impeccable recreation

00:05:33.260 --> 00:05:35.480
complete
with an official serial code and everything!

00:05:35.500 --> 00:05:37.130
So you're saying it's a fake?

00:05:37.130 --> 00:05:38.630
Oh no, no, no, no!

00:05:38.630 --> 00:05:41.750
The value of art lays in the piece itself,
not in its authenticity!

00:05:41.750 --> 00:05:44.710
This will one day fetch a 
high price! I guarantee it!

00:05:44.710 --> 00:05:48.070
Enough of this non-sense!
This thing is nothing but a bunch of scribbles!

00:05:48.070 --> 00:05:50.790
I wouldn't even trade a paper plane for that!

00:05:52.750 --> 00:05:54.130
So be it, then.

00:05:54.130 --> 00:05:55.200
We'll try again some other time.

00:05:55.200 --> 00:05:56.830
Y-you will?

00:05:56.830 --> 00:05:59.420
This was quite the sudden request, after all.

00:05:59.420 --> 00:06:02.040
It's only natural that you might want
some time to think it over.

00:06:08.500 --> 00:06:09.970
What a relief!

00:06:09.970 --> 00:06:12.960
Thank goodness they were so understanding.

00:06:12.040 --> 00:06:15.670
A bitter picaresque

00:06:15.670 --> 00:06:19.250
The bloody gore sticks 
never to be wiped clean

00:06:16.640 --> 00:06:17.380
Wait!

00:06:19.670 --> 00:06:23.250
Wherever you hide we will find you

00:06:23.250 --> 00:06:26.790
It's your own fault

00:06:29.420 --> 00:06:33.080
Oh we are a corporation, 
we'd never rip you off

00:06:30.330 --> 00:06:31.630
That's what you get!

00:06:31.630 --> 00:06:34.920
See, our policy with clients who
don't seem to see the value of our offers...

00:06:33.080 --> 00:06:37.920
Come along prepare to be 
duped, instead we are elite

00:06:34.920 --> 00:06:37.540
is to give them a crash course in "trade"!

00:06:37.540 --> 00:06:40.500
Now then, we'll be back in three days
with our entire staff!

00:06:37.920 --> 00:06:41.290
Elite industries

00:06:40.500 --> 00:06:43.460
So you'd best think this over 
real well, you lousy louses!

00:06:43.460 --> 00:06:45.840
We won't take no for an answer!

00:06:45.840 --> 00:06:47.970
So what was that about 
"bravely fighting," then?

00:06:47.970 --> 00:06:49.960
You guys didn't even try!

00:06:50.710 --> 00:06:52.290
Wait, but a Raiden, though?

00:06:52.290 --> 00:06:53.930
Since when did you guys have 
something like that here?

00:06:53.930 --> 00:06:56.330
Wow, so that's a Raiden?

00:06:56.330 --> 00:06:57.700
1800 horsepower.

00:06:57.700 --> 00:07:00.560
50 kilometers per hour faster
than the Hayabusa. Sporting four 20mm cannons.

00:07:00.580 --> 00:07:03.880
But that all makes it so sluggish.
I can't say I care for them.

00:07:03.880 --> 00:07:06.540
This has been passed down as
the mayor's personal craft, hasn't it?

00:07:06.540 --> 00:07:08.040
What?! You can fly?

00:07:08.040 --> 00:07:09.880
I used to be a pilot, you know!

00:07:09.880 --> 00:07:12.830
Back in the day people used to call me
the Prince of the Rahama skies-

00:07:11.290 --> 00:07:12.960
Yeah, yeah... maybe once 
upon a time, you were.

00:07:12.830 --> 00:07:14.330
What about those pirates, though?

00:07:14.330 --> 00:07:15.330
They'll be back in three days, right?

00:07:15.330 --> 00:07:16.710
Count me in!

00:07:16.710 --> 00:07:18.120
Wait, are you serious?

00:07:18.120 --> 00:07:20.960
Well, it's not like these guys can handle it!

00:07:20.960 --> 00:07:22.790
They'd be easy pickings for those pirates!

00:07:22.790 --> 00:07:24.170
Doesn't that just drive you mad?

00:07:24.170 --> 00:07:25.710
Sure, it does.

00:07:25.710 --> 00:07:30.130
But if they can't fight back themselves,
how would handing over one fighter hurt?

00:07:30.130 --> 00:07:31.580
It's not like you use it anyway, right?

00:07:31.580 --> 00:07:32.790
That's not a bad idea, huh!

00:07:32.790 --> 00:07:33.680
What?! But Mayor!

00:07:33.680 --> 00:07:38.580
I mean, it's a valuable fighter for sure,
but it's still just one plane, right?

00:07:38.580 --> 00:07:41.980
If we try fighting, who knows
what will happen to the town?

00:07:41.980 --> 00:07:43.150
You get a big nope from me!

00:07:43.150 --> 00:07:45.020
What? What's the big deal?

00:07:45.020 --> 00:07:49.210
I agree with Kylie.
A single craft is not worth risking the entire town.

00:07:49.210 --> 00:07:51.530
Don't go getting ahead 
of yourselves, girlies.

00:07:51.530 --> 00:07:54.960
We work for the Ouni Company now.
 The Madame is the only one who

00:07:54.960 --> 00:07:56.280
gets to make these decisions.

00:07:57.040 --> 00:08:01.570
If you want to use the KOTOBUKI 
Flight Corps to defend the town,

00:08:01.570 --> 00:08:04.500
I must ask that you speak to me, first.

00:08:05.130 --> 00:08:09.840
And the young ladies here will require contracts
and compensation, of course.

00:08:10.150 --> 00:08:12.020
How much might that cost, if I may-

00:08:12.020 --> 00:08:14.430
That's ridiculous! We don't 
have that kind of money!

00:08:14.430 --> 00:08:17.330
Fine! We don't need help from 
the likes of you, anyway!

00:08:17.330 --> 00:08:18.920
We'll take them on all by ourselves!

00:08:18.540 --> 00:08:19.250
What?!

00:08:18.920 --> 00:08:19.880
How?

00:08:19.880 --> 00:08:22.140
With sheer guts! Right?

00:08:22.140 --> 00:08:24.330
Mr. Mayor, we must request their services.

00:08:24.330 --> 00:08:26.460
Hey, are you sure that's okay for you to say?

00:08:26.460 --> 00:08:29.690
They said they had a fleet of 40 aircraft.

00:08:29.690 --> 00:08:32.630
All we have are eleven Type 97 fighters.

00:08:32.630 --> 00:08:35.990
Even assuming we were matched in skill,
we'd hardly stand a chance.

00:08:35.990 --> 00:08:38.200
We have anti-aircraft 
artillery, but we haven't

00:08:38.200 --> 00:08:40.200
had carried out proper 
training in over five years.

00:08:40.550 --> 00:08:42.830
Considering the current state 
of our vigilante force,

00:08:42.830 --> 00:08:44.990
I believe we'd be best off with their help.

00:08:44.990 --> 00:08:46.040
Please, just say the word.

00:08:46.040 --> 00:08:47.460
I can't do that, though!

00:08:47.460 --> 00:08:50.290
I can't just make these decisions on my own!

00:08:50.290 --> 00:08:51.710
Especially with the elections coming up...

00:08:51.710 --> 00:08:53.000
Mr. Mayor!

00:08:54.800 --> 00:08:56.040
All right, then!

00:08:56.040 --> 00:08:59.830
Let's hold a town meeting and
hear what everyone else has to say!

00:09:00.250 --> 00:09:02.130
You really don't want to make
this decision yourself, do you?

00:09:02.130 --> 00:09:04.040
I'm no dictator!

00:09:04.040 --> 00:09:06.020
The Magnificent
KOTOBUKI

00:09:06.630 --> 00:09:08.170
We should fight 'em off to the bitter end!

00:09:07.210 --> 00:09:08.500
Hear, hear!

00:09:08.170 --> 00:09:08.830
But still...

00:09:08.830 --> 00:09:10.630
That Raiden is our town's guardian angel!

00:09:10.630 --> 00:09:13.040
Rahama would be left with nothing but shame
if we let it be taken away!

00:09:13.040 --> 00:09:14.630
Who even believes in angels anymore?

00:09:14.630 --> 00:09:16.210
Fighting back will only 
cause trouble for the town.

00:09:16.210 --> 00:09:17.630
You're gonna let the pirates win?!

00:09:16.580 --> 00:09:18.130
And we've got public finances to consider...

00:09:18.250 --> 00:09:20.170
Then we should just set up 
a special tax or something!

00:09:18.380 --> 00:09:19.290
But still!

00:09:20.170 --> 00:09:22.000
More taxes?! You gotta be kidding!

00:09:21.000 --> 00:09:23.080
What's the vigilante force even doing?

00:09:22.000 --> 00:09:23.500
The town is in crisis!

00:09:22.000 --> 00:09:23.500
Quit trying to downplay this!

00:09:23.500 --> 00:09:28.130
You know, I always thought that
growing old also meant growing wiser, too.

00:09:28.130 --> 00:09:29.920
Age and intelligence do not 
increase proportionally.

00:09:29.920 --> 00:09:32.080
The Madame's sure heartless though, huh?

00:09:32.080 --> 00:09:34.170
Reona's her usual stubborn self, too.

00:09:34.170 --> 00:09:35.560
Can't they just stop thinking about the money

00:09:35.560 --> 00:09:37.620
and do something to help 
out the town for once?

00:09:37.620 --> 00:09:38.720
What a bunch of cheapskates!

00:09:38.720 --> 00:09:41.700
I bet they're calling you a

00:09:41.700 --> 00:09:45.810
cold-hearted, miserly, cheapskate, 
stubborn witch right about now.

00:09:46.170 --> 00:09:48.580
That's all just part of being in charge.

00:09:48.580 --> 00:09:51.790
My, my. You sure have it rough,
don't you, miss squad leader?

00:09:51.790 --> 00:09:53.250
Can I ask you for a moment?

00:09:55.380 --> 00:09:57.630
I think our discussions have 
reached their conclusion, so-

00:09:57.630 --> 00:09:58.630
No, they haven't!

00:09:58.630 --> 00:09:59.710
Yes, they have.

00:09:59.710 --> 00:10:02.210
You can't just ask for the impossible.

00:10:02.210 --> 00:10:05.110
We wouldn't even be having this 
discussion if the vigilantes

00:10:05.110 --> 00:10:07.040
weren't so useless to begin with!

00:10:07.220 --> 00:10:13.250
Right, so I'm thinking we will accept the offer
by Elite Industries, but what do you say?

00:10:13.250 --> 00:10:14.710
You're a bunch of fools.

00:10:14.710 --> 00:10:15.750
Emma?

00:10:15.750 --> 00:10:17.670
So much so, it honestly 
makes me sick to my stomach.

00:10:17.670 --> 00:10:19.130
You're dealing with air pirates.

00:10:19.130 --> 00:10:21.750
Do you truly think when you hand 
over your Raiden that they

00:10:21.750 --> 00:10:23.010
will simply pack up and leave?

00:10:23.750 --> 00:10:24.750
You don't think they will?

00:10:24.750 --> 00:10:26.180
This is just standard fare for them.

00:10:26.180 --> 00:10:29.540
They start you off with demands
just tough enough to still be swallow-able.

00:10:29.540 --> 00:10:34.420
But once you do, they come back
with even greater demands.

00:10:34.420 --> 00:10:37.920
And they do it again, and again, and again.

00:10:37.920 --> 00:10:40.620
With their demands getting worse every time.

00:10:40.620 --> 00:10:43.880
And before you know it,
you have nothing left for them to even ask for.

00:10:43.880 --> 00:10:46.290
Yeah, I'm with Emma on this one!

00:10:46.290 --> 00:10:47.630
Let's fight 'em off, people!

00:10:47.630 --> 00:10:48.120
Yeah!

00:10:48.120 --> 00:10:50.670
Mr. Mayor, they're right.

00:10:50.670 --> 00:10:53.170
The only way we can ensure the safety
of this town is to fight back!

00:10:53.170 --> 00:10:55.550
Maybe we should just call for
a recess to think things over-

00:10:55.550 --> 00:10:57.960
And you claim to be in charge of this town?

00:10:57.960 --> 00:11:01.000
A leader who avoids making decisions
like this is no leader at all!

00:11:01.000 --> 00:11:03.010
Do us all a favor and drop 
dead for us here now, then!

00:11:03.960 --> 00:11:07.630
Trust me, if we could make it work,
I'd rather fight back, too!

00:11:07.630 --> 00:11:12.630
But even if everyone here agreed,
our budget simply doesn't!

00:11:12.630 --> 00:11:15.380
You're certain you want to fight, then?

00:11:15.960 --> 00:11:17.670
I'm here with an offer 
from the Madame herself.

00:11:17.670 --> 00:11:20.460
If I'm being honest with you, this is too big of
a task for the KOTOBUKI Flight Corps alone.

00:11:20.790 --> 00:11:24.670
But she says if everyone in town is willing to help,
perhaps we can lend a hand.

00:11:24.670 --> 00:11:27.920
And if you do, she'll cut you a fine deal.

00:11:27.920 --> 00:11:32.420
Yeah... Back in the day we all used
to keep this place safe together.

00:11:32.420 --> 00:11:33.610
So that's what we gotta do!

00:11:33.610 --> 00:11:36.110
We all gotta stand up, so no one 
thinks they can take advantage of us!

00:11:36.110 --> 00:11:37.750
Mr. Mayor, it's time to make a decision.

00:11:37.750 --> 00:11:38.610
Mr. Mayor!

00:11:38.610 --> 00:11:39.670
Mr. Mayor!

00:11:39.670 --> 00:11:40.710
Mr. Mayor!

00:11:42.830 --> 00:11:44.430
All right! Then we fight!

00:12:09.250 --> 00:12:12.170
These "Elites" sure are 
taking their time, huh?

00:12:12.170 --> 00:12:16.170
Any chance they might have thought
things over and changed their minds?

00:12:16.630 --> 00:12:17.670
No, huh?

00:12:18.580 --> 00:12:19.920
I know, I know!

00:12:23.380 --> 00:12:24.790
This is Red Dragonfly Three!

00:12:24.790 --> 00:12:27.350
I've got eyes on enemy fighters coming
in from the north-northwest!

00:12:27.350 --> 00:12:28.500
From the opposite direction?!

00:12:28.500 --> 00:12:30.080
That's not how this was supposed to play out!

00:12:30.080 --> 00:12:31.370
We misread our enemy,

00:12:31.370 --> 00:12:34.080
and they're now moving in from the 
opposite direction of the KOTOBUKI squad.

00:12:34.080 --> 00:12:36.210
Which means we'll be taking the lead!

00:12:36.830 --> 00:12:39.080
It'll be fifteen minutes 
till they make it back.

00:12:39.080 --> 00:12:41.130
We need to hold them off until then!

00:12:41.130 --> 00:12:45.080
Bring 'em on! Let's show 'em what
we vigilantes are made of!

00:12:45.080 --> 00:12:46.330
That's the spirit!

00:12:46.330 --> 00:12:47.920
But don't let it get to your head!

00:12:47.920 --> 00:12:50.040
And don't let them scare you off, either!

00:12:50.040 --> 00:12:52.130
Rahama Vigilantes, take off!

00:13:10.460 --> 00:13:12.170
Here come their fighters.

00:13:12.170 --> 00:13:14.080
They're looking for a fight!

00:13:14.080 --> 00:13:17.390
The nerve. And here I was ready to compromise

00:13:17.390 --> 00:13:21.610
and offer them another 
ukiyo-e to seal the deal!

00:13:22.290 --> 00:13:25.740
How dare they turn down our 
boss- our CEO's kindness!

00:13:25.740 --> 00:13:26.990
They must pay for this!

00:13:26.990 --> 00:13:28.040
They will!

00:13:28.040 --> 00:13:32.080
Spare no sympathy for the sorts that
can't see how much our art is worth!

00:13:32.080 --> 00:13:34.670
HR department! Swat down those flies!

00:13:34.670 --> 00:13:38.330
Sales team, light up all their infrastructure
to teach them a lesson!

00:13:38.330 --> 00:13:41.170
But don't you even put a dent on that Raiden!

00:13:41.170 --> 00:13:42.500
Aye aye, sir!

00:13:42.500 --> 00:13:43.500
They're splitting up!

00:13:43.500 --> 00:13:46.210
They might have the numbers,
but we have greater firepower!

00:13:46.210 --> 00:13:48.130
Don't let them shoot you down!

00:13:58.420 --> 00:14:00.710
Here's what you get for breaking 
the code of the trade.

00:14:05.420 --> 00:14:06.960
What the heck?!

00:14:06.960 --> 00:14:10.040
They've got the Raiden out 
right in the middle of town!

00:14:10.040 --> 00:14:11.960
Go on and shoot if you like!

00:14:10.500 --> 00:14:11.420
Idiots!

00:14:11.420 --> 00:14:12.500
Go on then, you stinkin' pirates!

00:14:12.500 --> 00:14:13.250
Fire!

00:14:18.870 --> 00:14:21.130
Dangit! They aren't making this easy!

00:14:58.410 --> 00:14:59.750
Damn!

00:15:04.880 --> 00:15:05.920
Wait! Cap'n!

00:15:05.920 --> 00:15:08.630
You idiot. Getting all worked up
only means you've already lost.

00:15:08.630 --> 00:15:09.290
Get 'em!

00:15:12.180 --> 00:15:13.380
Cap'n!

00:15:16.720 --> 00:15:18.460
Out of my way, you.

00:15:21.380 --> 00:15:22.750
Tokiwagi!

00:15:30.250 --> 00:15:31.350
KOTOBUKI!

00:15:31.350 --> 00:15:32.880
Good work holding them off!

00:15:32.880 --> 00:15:33.960
We'll take things from here!

00:15:34.330 --> 00:15:35.580
Stick to the plan.

00:15:35.580 --> 00:15:39.040
Chika and Kate along with
Zara and I will pick them off from up here.

00:15:39.380 --> 00:15:41.290
Kylie and Emma, you two work
with everyone on the ground!

00:15:41.290 --> 00:15:42.040
Roger that!

00:15:45.750 --> 00:15:47.840
I'm not gonna lose out to another Hayabusa!

00:15:48.070 --> 00:15:50.600
The Type-3 can fly 30 kilometers 
per hour faster than the Type-1,

00:15:50.600 --> 00:15:51.930
so if they shake us we can't catch up.

00:15:51.930 --> 00:15:53.380
Like I care!

00:15:59.560 --> 00:16:00.420
Gotcha!

00:16:10.210 --> 00:16:10.710
All right!

00:16:19.380 --> 00:16:20.580
Oh no, you don't!

00:16:51.170 --> 00:16:52.460
What's the deal with these guys?

00:16:52.460 --> 00:16:54.170
Perhaps it's the KOTOBUKI Flight Corps?

00:16:54.170 --> 00:16:56.290
Hmph, like we don't have 
enough enemies already.

00:16:56.290 --> 00:16:57.420
Take 'em out!

00:17:00.330 --> 00:17:02.500
Stop aiming at them!
You need to anticipate their movements!

00:17:22.460 --> 00:17:23.790
Emma, it's time to do this!

00:17:23.790 --> 00:17:24.890
You don't need to tell me!

00:17:44.630 --> 00:17:46.630
How dare you shoot down our sales chief!

00:18:04.680 --> 00:18:06.750
You little...! You're going down!

00:18:13.420 --> 00:18:14.960
There they go! They're yours!

00:18:14.960 --> 00:18:16.210
Very well, then!

00:18:30.460 --> 00:18:31.330
Fire!

00:18:39.300 --> 00:18:40.420
Nice! It worked!

00:18:40.420 --> 00:18:41.600
We aren't finished yet.

00:18:55.900 --> 00:18:57.990
How dare you treat my lovely staff this way!

00:18:57.990 --> 00:18:58.630
Emma!

00:18:58.630 --> 00:18:59.750
I won't go down that easy...

00:19:10.790 --> 00:19:11.960
A rear gunner?!

00:19:14.590 --> 00:19:15.340
Emma!

00:19:22.680 --> 00:19:23.830
Time to boost our results!

00:19:31.540 --> 00:19:33.250
Not on my watch!

00:19:35.440 --> 00:19:36.290
The Raiden?!

00:19:42.630 --> 00:19:45.880
Don't you underestimate the 
Prince of the Rahama skies!

00:19:48.080 --> 00:19:51.210
Dammit! Listen up!
Don't you dare shoot down that Raiden!

00:19:51.210 --> 00:19:52.130
They aren't shooting back?

00:19:52.130 --> 00:19:53.790
This might be crazy enough to work!

00:19:53.790 --> 00:19:54.540
Emma!

00:19:54.540 --> 00:19:56.500
Emma!

00:20:09.460 --> 00:20:10.290
Emma!

00:20:10.710 --> 00:20:11.670
I'm all right.

00:20:12.250 --> 00:20:13.420
And I'm sorry...

00:20:13.420 --> 00:20:14.330
Why you...!

00:20:14.330 --> 00:20:15.250
You...!

00:20:28.080 --> 00:20:29.830
Special delivery!

00:20:31.290 --> 00:20:32.790
Pleasure doing business with ya!

00:20:32.790 --> 00:20:34.250
All right, fall back!

00:20:34.250 --> 00:20:35.170
Aye aye, sir!

00:20:44.460 --> 00:20:45.460
Can anyone keep on them?!

00:20:45.460 --> 00:20:47.350
It's too late, and I'm out of ammo.

00:20:51.250 --> 00:20:52.290
Pull up.

00:20:52.290 --> 00:20:55.750
Everyone fought together and
still this is how things end?!

00:20:55.750 --> 00:20:57.500
The town's in pretty bad shape, too.

00:20:57.960 --> 00:21:00.670
Maybe they really should have
just handed it over to begin with.

00:21:00.670 --> 00:21:02.000
Far from it.

00:21:02.500 --> 00:21:06.460
Rahama has shown that we have what it takes
to work together to take on any air pirates.

00:21:06.460 --> 00:21:09.580
I doubt they'll show their faces
around here again for a while.

00:21:09.580 --> 00:21:11.580
This is the sort of wake up call I needed.

00:21:11.580 --> 00:21:14.420
To remind me what it really 
means to protect the town.

00:21:31.540 --> 00:21:34.000
I'm sorry for being such a worthless mayor.

00:21:34.000 --> 00:21:37.500
Oh no. I must thank you for coming to my aid.

00:21:37.920 --> 00:21:40.830
Please forgive me for
my crude speech last night, as well.

00:21:41.750 --> 00:21:47.790
Still, the contracts you signed with the town
included a clause about protecting the Raiden.

00:21:48.210 --> 00:21:49.580
You do understand what this means, yes?

00:21:49.580 --> 00:21:50.290
Of course.

00:21:50.710 --> 00:21:51.670
Good.

00:21:52.080 --> 00:21:54.540
Now go on out there and 
get that fighter back!

00:21:54.540 --> 00:21:55.540
Yes, ma'am!

00:22:04.540 --> 00:22:08.630
I wanted to try and soar through that sky

00:22:08.630 --> 00:22:12.460
So I wished upon the winds right before me

00:22:12.460 --> 00:22:16.380
Our aspirations build us scenery

00:22:16.380 --> 00:22:20.790
I wonder how that wind is now

00:22:25.040 --> 00:22:29.130
Why do we fight, I wonder

00:22:29.130 --> 00:22:33.170
What is our purpose here?

00:22:33.170 --> 00:22:41.420
I asked, but the skies do not answer

00:22:42.130 --> 00:22:49.080
We all have wings

00:22:49.080 --> 00:22:53.790
Far away at the end of all lament

00:22:53.790 --> 00:22:58.040
The stories we found

00:22:58.040 --> 00:23:05.790
No one can steal these skies away

00:23:05.960 --> 00:23:10.500
We will soar unafraid of anything

00:23:10.500 --> 00:23:17.670
Because happiness is right here

00:23:26.080 --> 00:23:27.540
Preview

00:23:33.290 --> 00:23:37.290
Next time on The Magnificent KOTOBUKI,
"Elite Fortress"!

00:23:38.290 --> 00:23:41.040
Elite Fortress
